// LithosAI's hosted inference engine (api.lithosai.cloud): one
// OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint serving open-weight models —
// Kimi K3, DeepSeek V4.1 Flash, GLM-5.3 — at full precision on the operator's
// own GPUs. The roster is account-scoped ("Lists the models your organization
// can call"), so `GET /v1/models` answers 401 `invalid API key` without a
// credential, and with one it publishes bare `{id, object, created, owned_by}`
// rows: no limits, tariffs, or capability metadata. Nothing about a row is
// therefore discoverable, and no rows are frozen here.
//
// Deliberately no `discovery` node: that node enrolls a provider in
// generate-models.ts, which would demand a live account credential on every
// regeneration and freeze one organization's roster into models.json.
// `dynamic-models-authoritative` prunes rows the roster drops.
//
// The wire facts below are transcribed from the vendor's published OpenAPI
// document (docs.lithosai.com/openapi.yaml, `info.version: 2026-09-17`), not
// from a live probe: the account used to read the roster carried no credit, so
// every chat completion answered 402 `insufficient_quota` before any request
// field could be exercised. Fields the schema documents are declared; anything
// the schema is silent about is left at the openai-completions default.
//
// The roster names each model family in base, `-fast`, `-ultra` and
// `-ultra-chat` tiers (13 ids over three families as of 2026-10-03). The
// vendor prices base/fast/ultra as the same weights served at different
// speeds, and nothing published defines what `-chat` changes, so no rule here
// names a tier.
provider "lithosai" {
	default-model "moonshotai/Kimi-K3"
	env "LITHOSAI_API_KEY"
	dynamic-models-authoritative #true

	// Request schema: `max_tokens` and `max_completion_tokens` are both
	// accepted, `reasoning_effort` takes a named effort string, and the
	// response message and streamed delta both carry `reasoning_content`.
	// `role` enumerates `developer`; `store` is not a documented field.
	max-tokens-field "max_tokens"
	thinking-mode "effort"
	reasoning-content-field "reasoning_content"
	supports-developer-role #true
	supports-store #false
}
